{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>their portion — I have given it from My fire-offerings</b> — for even in the matter of dividing they are not permitted [to take] except after the gifts of the fire, and from here we learn [this rule] for all consecrated offerings, as it is written: \"it is most holy\" (Torat Kohanim, chapter 3:2). And \"it shall not be baked leavened — their portion\": that even the remnant is forbidden in leavening (Menahot 55a). And \"like the sin-offering and like the guilt-offering\" teaches: just as the sin-offering [is eaten] from unconsecrated [funds], by day, and with the right hand, so too this one [is taken] from unconsecrated [funds], by day, and with the right hand (Torat Kohanim 3:3). \"Every male among the sons of Aaron\" — that even priests with blemishes share in the portion (Zevahim 98a). And it adds concerning the priests: \"And every meal-offering of a priest shall be wholly burned; it shall not be eaten\" (Leviticus 6:16). And the Rav said in the Guide for the Perplexed (III:46) that the reason is that every priest who offers his offering does so on his own behalf, and if he were to offer a meal-offering and eat it himself, it would be as though he had not offered anything at all — for from an individual's meal-offering he offers from it nothing but the frankincense and the handful, and this meager offering would not suffice, so that he might eat it and it would seem as though he had not offered a sacrifice at all. Therefore they must burn all of it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:50:52.858309318Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}